xocs:item-toc-entry.xocs:item-toc-section-title:
Anaerobic biodegradability (ABD

                     v
                  ) of vinasse and the energy extraction efficiency

ce:section.ce:para:
The OLR increase by reducing the HRT of the UASB reactors and the addition of NaHCO3 to the influent of the reactors had a strong influence on methane production (Fig. 3
                        , Tables 2 and 3
                        ). After influent buffering, the methane content of the biogas increased from approximately 17% (both reactors) to 61% (UASB I) and 68.8% (UASB II). Methane production and methane yield increased with the increase of the OLR (15–25 kg-COD m−3 d−1) as presented in Fig. 3A–D. Furthermore, volumetric methane production (VMP) was higher in UASB II, indicating that acidogenic phase separation increased the energy extraction, which was confirmed by examining the methane yield values of 234.2 NmL-CH4.g−1CODremoved and 306 NmL-CH4 g−1CODremoved at the end of the operation of UASB I and UASB II, respectively. Considering the maximum theoretical yield of methane (350 NmL-CH4.g−1COD), this value was 87.4% of the maximum theoretical yield of methane, which is similar to Souza et al. [12] and Harada et al. [13].

